{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Review remediation (2026-08-21) — narration moved out of the description to keep it under the\nplan-review admission limit. What was factually wrong in the original plan and what was corrected,\nwith file:line evidence.\n\n1. The rule could not be computed where the plan put it.\n   `registry.content_triggered_overlays` (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py:416`) takes only\n   `(diff_text, repo_root)` and is path-blind by construction — every helper skips the `+++`/`---`\n   headers — so the \"changes no file under `tests/**`\" half of the trigger had no operand there. The\n   corrected plan adds a keyword-only `changed_files: Sequence[str] = ()` (existing call sites and\n   tests keep working positionally) and passes the step's `changed` list at\n   `src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py:99`.\n\n2. The scanned text is not a raw diff. The step receives\n   `steps.assemble_diff.outputs.context` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml:64`,\n   `:118`), i.e. the COMPOSED context: a `## Changed files` list plus orientation plus the diff,\n   truncated at `DIFF_CHAR_CAP = 60000` (`assemble.py:30`, `compose_diff_context` `:78-93`). An\n   added definition past the cap therefore does not trigger — recorded as a blind spot — and both\n   shapes (raw diff and composed context) are now exercised in tests. `changed_files` is unaffected\n   by truncation, which is why the negative half of the rule is keyed on it.\n\n3. Gerrit 1547 (`24917e843b`) was miscounted. Its `src/` delta has 0 added `def`/`class` lines and 0\n   added branch lines, and it also changed four docs files, so the original \"five src-only changes\n   all select\" acceptance criterion was unsatisfiable. 1547 is now an explicit NEGATIVE case.\n\n4. The corpus shapes were mischaracterised. Gerrit 1920 (`721cb7d6ac`) and 1737 (`1c2bf6e57b`) are\n   pure MOVES, and 1703 (`83d91d488c`) is an annotation-only signature rewrite — contradicting the\n   plan's claim that \"pure renames add no definitions and never trigger\". Moves now trigger by\n   design; annotation-only rewrites are suppressed explicitly.\n\n5. Rename detection is OFF in the reviewed diff. The gate composes `git diff base...head` with no\n   `-M` (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py:230`), so a rename reaches the reviewer as delete +\n   add. The old `git diff -M` rename-only edge case tested a shape production never sends.\n\n6. Two code citations were wrong: `content_triggered_overlays` is at `registry.py:416`, not `:413`;\n   guard (vii) is at `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md:97` — `:73-75` is the\n   Four-Criterion Test bullet, which the plan leaves unchanged.\n\n7. `tests/unit/llm/` does not exist. Both the proposed new test path and the\n   `tests/unit/llm/code_review/test_registry*.py` pinning path were unreachable. The flat\n   `tests/unit/test_code_review_*.py` layout and the real pinning suites\n   (`test_code_review_triggers.py`, `test_code_review_deletion_impact.py`,\n   `test_code_review_evals.py`) are named instead.\n\n8. The prompt edit has wider blast radius than stated. Guard (vii) lives in ONE prompt shared by\n   Round-A and Round-B, so narrowing it changes blocking eligibility for the whole existing\n   glob-triggered population (calibrated at 0.54, \"blocks 99 changes / 8.0%\"), not only the new\n   content-triggered one. That is now stated as intended, with a matching pre-existing-code FP case\n   added to the eval corpus.\n\n9. Two consumers were unlisted. `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml` — the\n   calibration corpus the routing `_comment` names, already carrying `R-missing-regression-test` —\n   is now in Scope; the `tests`-keyed Pass-4 coach moves (`moves.py:26-31`, `:74-84`), which will\n   now offer on ordinary src changes, are recorded as an accepted consequence. Round-A is uncapped\n   (`cap: 3` exists only on the Round-B `union` step, `code-review.yaml:118`), so each qualifying\n   change costs one extra frontier overlay call.\n\n10. No project overlay could express this trigger. `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` has no `tests`\n    entry, and `registry.project_trigger_extensions` (`registry.py:254`) supports only\n    literal-substring `trigger_tokens` and additive `applies_to` globs — neither can express \"adds a\n    definition AND touches no `tests/**`\". Hence the committed detector."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787371446999092001,"uuid":"7ed961ca-cee3-495b-9de2-5ea98fba2972"}